visible rather than implied.


Elite Dangerous game data
-------------------------

Directive 47 was created using assets and imagery from Elite Dangerous, with the
permission of Frontier Developments plc, for non-commercial purposes. It is not
endorsed by nor reflects the views or opinions of Frontier Developments and no
employee of Frontier Developments was involved in the making of it.

That is Frontier's own long-form attribution, from the Elite Dangerous Media Usage
Rules:

    https://forums.frontier.co.uk/threads/elite-dangerous-media-usage-rules.510879/

Those rules permit non-commercial community projects to use Frontier's game content
provided it is clearly attributed, and require written permission for commercial use.
**Directive 47 is non-commercial.** The MIT licence above covers the code; it is not
a grant of any right over Frontier's game data, and anyone reusing this project is
bound by Frontier's rules independently of it.

The following shipped tables contain game data derived under those rules. Each is
generated by a script in tools/, never hand-written, and each records the source it
was derived from in its own header:

    src/D47.Core/Journal/MaterialGrades.g.cs        tools/gen-material-grades.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/EliteSpecifications.tsv  tools/gen-elite-specs.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/Engineers.tsv            tools/gen-engineers.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/SystemNames.tsv          tools/gen-system-names.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/Exobiology.tsv           tools/gen-exobiology.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/GuardianSites.tsv        tools/gen-guardian-sites.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/Regions.tsv              tools/gen-regions.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/Codex.tsv                tools/gen-codex.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/PowerplayRanks.tsv       tools/gen-powerplay.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/LandingPads.tsv          tools/gen-landing-pads.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/Missions.tsv             tools/gen-missions.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/StepEvents.tsv           tools/gen-step-events.py
    src/D47.Core/Knowledge/StepFields.tsv           tools/gen-step-events.py
    assets/engineers/                               tools/gen-engineer-portraits.py

The pictures in assets/engineers/ are the page images of the engineers' articles on the
Elite Dangerous Wiki (Fandom), saved by hand from each article and cropped by
tools/gen-engineer-portraits.py. They are Frontier's in-game imagery under the rules
quoted above. The wiki's CC BY-SA licence covers its text and does not cover them.


Community data sources
----------------------

These supply the ids, names and figures the generators above join together. Their own
licences are recorded here; none of them conveys rights over the underlying game data,
which remains Frontier's in every case.

    EDCD/FDevIDs           No licence file. The canonical community id list, and the
                           source of the symbols the journal writes.

    EDCD/coriolis-data     Code MIT. Its LICENSE.md states that the data and JSON
                           files are the intellectual property of Frontier
                           Developments plc.

    msarilar/EDEngineer    MIT.

    jixxed/ed-odyssey-     MIT. src/D47.Core/Knowledge/OnFoot.tsv takes one English sentence
    materials-helper       per on-foot modification, saying what it does, from its
                           description.csv; tools/gen-onfoot.py writes it into the detail
                           column.
                           src/D47.Core/Knowledge/MaterialTraders.tsv is generated by
                           tools/gen-material-traders.py from its traders.jsonl.

    klightspeed/           MIT. src/D47.Core/Knowledge/Regions.tsv is generated by
    EliteDangerousRegionMap tools/gen-regions.py from its RegionMapData.json, and
                           GalacticRegions.Find ports its FindRegion algorithm; both state which of
                           the 42 codex regions a position falls in, which is Frontier's game data
                           under the rules quoted above.

    canonn-science/        MIT. src/D47.Core/Knowledge/Codex.tsv is generated by tools/gen-codex.py
    Dumpr                  from the codex extracts Dumpr writes daily, which its README allows
                           third-party tools to use. The table lists the codex entries reported in
                           each galactic region; the names are Frontier's game data under the rules
                           quoted above. With Earlier biology finds on, the app asks
                           Canonn's query API for the codex entries logged in the system you are in.

    taleden/EDSY           Code CC BY-NC 4.0. Its header states that the Elite
                           Dangerous game logic and data in the file remain the
                           property of Frontier Developments plc, used under the same
                           Media Usage Rules quoted above. It is the source of the
                           per-hull slot layout — what the journal calls a slot before
                           anything is fitted to it — which neither source above
                           carries.

    EDSM nightly dumps     No licence published; the dumps page carries only a
                           copyright footer. src/D47.Core/Knowledge/SystemNames.tsv
                           is generated by tools/gen-system-names.py from
                           systemsPopulated.json.gz and takes system names only,
                           which are Frontier's game data under the rules quoted
                           above.

    spansh.co.uk           No licence published. src/D47.Core/Knowledge/Exobiology.tsv
                           is generated by tools/gen-exobiology.py from api/bodies/search,
                           and takes species names, sale values and the body conditions
                           they were surveyed under — Frontier's game data under the
                           rules quoted above. src/D47.Core/Knowledge/GuardianSites.tsv
                           is generated by tools/gen-guardian-sites.py from the same
                           search, and takes the system, its address and position, the
                           body, and whether the body holds a Guardian ruin or structure,
                           with the structure layouts the search names.
                           src/D47.Core/Knowledge/CodexBodies.tsv is generated by
                           tools/gen-codex-bodies.py from the galaxy dump
                           (downloads.spansh.co.uk/galaxy.json.gz), and takes body types
                           and the number of systems with each type per codex region —
                           Frontier's game data under the rules quoted above.

    Colony distances       ArtemisScannerTracker (https://github.com/Balvald/ArtemisScannerTracker,
                           organicinfo.py), HerzbubeWiki's EDExobiology page
                           (https://wiki.herzbube.ch/wiki/EDExobiology) and EDCoPilot's spoken
                           callouts. The colony_distance column of
                           src/D47.Core/Knowledge/Exobiology.tsv comes from COLONY_DISTANCES in
                           tools/curated_exobiology.py, which takes the metres per genus and
                           nothing else — Frontier's game data under the rules quoted above.

    CMDR Eralm_237         No licence published. src/D47.Core/Knowledge/PowerplayRanks.tsv
    (Powerplay rank sheet) is generated by tools/gen-powerplay.py from the sheet's twelve
                           Power tabs, and takes the merits each rank needs and what it
                           grants — Frontier's game data under the rules quoted above.

    jixxed/ed-journal-     Apache-2.0, at commit e4976b5f9b46f784029364453622c2668087cfd6.
    schemas                src/D47.Core/Knowledge/StepEvents.tsv and StepFields.tsv are
                           generated by tools/gen-step-events.py from its schemas, and take
                           event and field names, field types and the event descriptions.

    rdnt/ed-landing-pads   MIT. https://github.com/rdnt/ed-landing-pads
                           © 2018 Tasos Papalyras - All Rights Reserved.
                           src/D47.Core/Knowledge/LandingPads.tsv is generated by
                           tools/gen-landing-pads.py from the pad table in its index.html,
                           and takes each pad's segment, depth and size in a ring station —
                           Frontier's game data under the rules quoted above.

    EDSM-NET/Alias         No licence file. https://github.com/EDSM-NET/Alias
                           src/D47.Core/Knowledge/Missions.tsv is generated by
                           tools/gen-missions.py from the keys of Station/Mission/Type.php,
                           mission names only, never its display strings — Frontier's game
                           data under the rules quoted above.

Sources examined and deliberately not used are recorded, with the reasons, in
docs/spikes/README.md.


Catalogues read at runtime, never shipped
-----------------------------------------

    EDAstro Galactic        CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, (c) CMDR Orvidius. https://edastro.com/gec/
    Exploration Catalog     Read over the network, on request and behind a setting that is
                            off by default, when the ship's AI writes a short story (list.md
                            Phase 47). Nothing from it is stored in a table of d47's own:
                            the catalogue suggests places, the generated story names them,
                            and the descriptions are read as information. Directive 47 is
                            non-commercial, which is the condition the licence attaches.

    EDDN FSS signals        No licence published. Signals uploaded by Commanders to the
                            Elite Dangerous Data Network, read from its public daily archive
                            at https://edgalaxydata.space/ by tools/signal-index.py, which
                            publishes the daily index on the signals-1 release of this
                            repository. Downloaded over the network when a signal search asks
                            for it, behind a setting that is off by default. It holds system
                            names, positions and signal names, which are Frontier's game data
                            under the rules quoted above.


